+PROVED consequence: normalized circle convolution preserves f_A>=-M(A), so S_Y>=-2M(A)+1/2-F_Y/2. On Y^(-1/2)<=|x|<=pi, F_Y<=pi^2, giving S_Y>=-2M(A)-(pi^2-1)/2. This holds with no smoothing hypothesis and is enough for the proposed front reduction. The particular -4m error estimate in the brief has not been established by this identity; the safe statement uses the actual M(A).
