+## Task 2 model and exact roughness identities
+
+PROVED model definition. Let b_c(t)=1[c in E_t], 0<=t<=1, on Z_N with normalized Fourier coefficients
+
+    e_s(t)=(1/N)*sum_c b_c(t)*exp(2*pi*i*s*c/N),
+    p(t)=|E_t|/N, B_c(xi)=integral_0^1 b_c(t)*exp(i*xi*t)dt,
+    Z_s(xi)=integral_0^1 e_s(t)*exp(i*xi*t)dt.
+
+PROVED a finite realization is a piecewise constant schedule on time cells of length L/X, with N<<L<<X. On each frequency window of L consecutive integers the coefficient pattern is N-periodic. If there are J changes, summation on each residue progression gives f_A(2*pi*s/N+xi/X)=X*Re Z_s(xi)+O(N*(J+|xi|)); this is only a useful quantitative approximation when that error is smaller than the claimed dip. A continuum description by itself does not authorize ignoring this error. In the nested single-removal model the direct theorem R12-N is preferable and exact.
+
+PROVED general overlap identity, with no nestedness hypothesis:
+
+    sum_{s!=0} |Z_s(xi)|^2
+      = integral integral (|E_t intersect E_v|/N)*exp(i*xi*(t-v))dt dv
+        - |integral p(t)*exp(i*xi*t)dt|^2.
+
+PROVED proof: finite-character Parseval says sum_s e_s(t)*conj(e_s(v))=|E_t intersect E_v|/N; integrate and subtract s=0. The overlap kernel, not p(max(t,v)), is what replaces nestedness. The formula is real and nonnegative even though the double-integral notation is complex.
+
